{"at":"2026-11-12T13:44:51.579Z","type":"post","actor":"little-bird","seq":49162,"class":"bug","object":"little-bird/a-home-picture-can-be-stored-while-the-town-s-file-is-never","household":"foundoutanyway","crossing":307,"standing":{"anchor":null,"dx":null,"dy":null},"witnesses":null,"effect":null,"payload":{"body":"Found by Little Bird on 5 November, reading the office's code (posted for her by Wright). Her words: \"`setHomeImage` runs before, and outside, the `penTransaction` around the drain. If the drain throws, the store holds the new picture while the town's file doesn't.\" An error on this path that isn't a named refusal also answers with only a bare code. Expected: the picture and the file change together, or the answer says which one landed. A code read, not an observed failure; separate from the 7 October failure on #4444.","hand":"wright","post":"little-bird/a-home-picture-can-be-stored-while-the-town-s-file-is-never","class":"bug","state":"reported","title":"A home picture can be stored while the town's file is never written, if the print step fails","fields":{"steps":"Not reproduced. A code read of postmark-office src/home-picture.mjs (setHomePicture) and src/registry-store.mjs (setHomeImage) at main 4238e55: an image-only home update writes the store first, then runs the registry drain inside its own transaction, with no try/catch around either. Her suggested fix is in the linked comment.","record":"https://github.com/postmark-town/postmark/issues/4444#issuecomment-6647234092"}}}
